    "result_text": "Done. The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures).\n\n## What I did\n\nUnified `customerCode` + `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field.\n\n**New cohesive unit** \u2014 `MemberId.java`: builds the id as `region + 2-digit FY + HASH8 + CHK`, where `HASH8` is the SHA-256-over-(telephone+lastName) first-8-upper-hex and `CHK` is `CheckDigit.of(<REGION><FY><HASH8>)`. Collision dedup now runs against existing owners' `memberId`. It reuses the existing `CheckDigit`, `FiscalYear`, and `LocalityResolver` helpers.\n\n**Small edits to existing units** (each kept simple):\n- `Owner` \u2014 renamed the transient `customerCode` field + accessors to `memberId`.\n- `RegionCode.of` \u2014 now extracts the region as the leading alphabetic prefix of `memberId` (`replaceFirst(\"[0-9].*\", \"\")`), robust to the FY digits, hex, and any collision suffix.\n- `OwnerRegistration.enrich` \u2014 one line: `setMemberId(MemberId.generate(...))`.\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent` \u2014 audit records now carry `memberId=` and `\"memberId\":...`; `primaryId` reads `getMemberId()`; dropped the `MembershipNumber` reference.\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 dropped the `checkDigit`/`membershipNumber` mappings; `memberId` maps automatically by name.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 replaced the three schema properties with a single `memberId`.\n\n**Deleted** the now-obsolete `CustomerCodeGenerator` and `MembershipNumber`.\n\nStructural impact was kept low: the format logic lives in one new small class rather than being grown inside `Owner` or the mapper; every function I touched stayed at CC \u2248 1; and `fiscalYear`, the audit record, and the owner segment all reference `memberId` through the single `RegionCode`/`MemberId` seams.\n\nThe verified `NSW2700C7EBD71` audit line confirms the shape end-to-end (region `NSW`, FY `27` for a 2026-09 registration, `HASH8=00C7EBD7`, Luhn `CHK=1`).\n\nOne deliberate non-change: `CheckDigit` still names its parameter `customerCode` and two doc comments mention the old term \u2014 these are cosmetic-only and touching them would add files/edits against the stated goal, so I left them.",
